  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Hello! I am Lily. Look at the picture. This is my room. This is a bed. I sleep in my bed. The bed is small, but it is nice. This is a desk. The desk is next to the window. This is a lamp. The lamp is on the desk.",
      "Look at the picture again. This is a rug. The rug is green, and it is on the floor. This is a door. The door is open. Here are my crayons. They are on the desk, next to the lamp. I draw in my room. The window is big and open. I love my room!",
      "Now Tom asks, \"Is it correct?\" Say yes or no. \"The rug is on the floor.\" Yes, it is correct! \"The bed is in the kitchen.\" No, it is not correct. \"The lamp is on the floor.\" No, the lamp is on the desk. \"The crayons are on the desk.\" Yes, that is correct! Can you ask a question about my room?"
    ],
    "summary": "Lily shows the things in her room, one by one. At the end, you say if a sentence about the picture is correct.",
